From: xtandard-image
Subject: [PATCH] Refuse macroblock rows past the plane

Found by fuzzing (Go FuzzJXR, confirmed with ASan): PKImageDecode_Copy_WMP
asks the planar alpha plane for as many macroblock rows as the image has;
an alpha plane whose header declares fewer was decoded past its last row
and past its offset tables (heap over-read in outputNChannel). Fail the
decode instead.
---
--- a/image/decode/strdec.c
+++ b/image/decode/strdec.c
@@ -3498,6 +3498,11 @@
     cMBRow = (pSC->m_Dparam->bDecodeFullFrame ? pSC->cmbHeight : ((pSC->m_Dparam->cROIBottomY + 16) >> 4));
 
 #ifdef REENTRANT_MODE
+    // The caller counts rows from the image's height; a planar alpha plane
+    // whose own header is shorter would be decoded past its last row (and
+    // past its lookup tables). One row of delay is legitimate.
+    if (pSC->WMIBI.uiLastMBRow > cMBRow + 1)
+        return ICERR_ERROR;
     if (0 == pSC->WMIBI.uiFirstMBRow)
     {
         if(initLookupTables(pSC) != ICERR_OK)
